Create six coordinated XS Urkaaaz button backgrounds: three widths, each in
normal and pressed states. Keep them text-free so Android can render live
labels over them. Use the approved gold Loadout button family; do not introduce
a separate visual style for compact navigation such as `BACK`.

## Reference

- Attach the approved `loadout_start_match_button_xs_normal.png` and
  `loadout_start_match_button_xs_pressed.png` as the definitive visual and
  interaction-state references.
- Attach the Loadout screen screenshot to check how a compact button fits
  beside the existing header and content. Use it as a composition reference;
  labels rendered over these assets by the game must be dark and bold.
- Preserve the shared gold face, bronze bevels, silhouette language, and
  restrained highlights. The width changes; the button family does not.

## Output

- Generate exactly six separate transparent PNG files: one normal and one
  pressed background for each of the three XS widths. Do not render labels,
  letters, icons, or any other text into the PNGs.
- All canvases are RGBA PNGs rendered at 4x the target dp dimensions.

| Length | Target display size | PNG canvas size |
|---|---:|---:|
| Short | 96 x 32 dp | 384 x 128 px |
| Normal | 128 x 32 dp | 512 x 128 px |
| Long | 160 x 32 dp | 640 x 128 px |

- Filenames use the order `<size>_<length>_<interaction-state>`. Thus
  `xs_normal_normal` means XS size, Normal length, normal interaction state.
- Use these exact filenames:
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_short_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_short_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_normal_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_normal_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_long_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_long_pressed.png`
- Save all six files for review under `assets_src/loadout/ui/`.
- Do not copy these variants into Android resources until the user approves
  the preview.

## Shared visual design

- Keep the same warm-gold face, dark bronze/gold bevels, transparent outer
  margins, and restrained edge lighting as the approved XS reference.
- Keep the height, border thickness, corner treatment, lighting direction, and
  state styling consistent across all three widths.
- Adapt the center plate to each width instead of cropping the reference.
  Keep the side bevels and any diamond accents proportional and fully visible;
  do not squeeze the ornaments into the text-safe area.
- Keep the center area clear of ornaments so Android-rendered text can be
  centered on the gold face with strong contrast.
- The game renders these live labels in its existing typeface, bold and dark:
  Short `BACK`, Normal `NEXT LEVEL`, and Long `RESTART MATCH`. This mapping is
  contextual guidance only; do not include the labels in the PNG assets.
- Keep the gold treatment consistent for primary, secondary, and navigation
  actions. A compact `BACK` button may use the Short variant, but must not
  switch to a different color or unrelated button design.
- These button images are 32 dp high. The app must provide an accessible touch
  target separately when the background is used for an interactive control.

## Length variants

- **Short (96 x 32 dp):** leave a center area suitable for short labels such
  as `BACK`. Keep the side details small and outside the text area.
- **Normal (128 x 32 dp):** match the approved XS proportions and detailing;
  preserve room for a compact live label such as `NEXT LEVEL`.
- **Long (160 x 32 dp):** extend the center plate horizontally; do not enlarge
  the height or make the bevels look heavier; it supports a longer live label
  such as `RESTART MATCH`.
- All three sizes must look like the same button at different widths when
  displayed side by side.

## Interaction states

- **Normal:** bright raised gold face, crisp upper bevel, and a restrained
  outer highlight.
- **Pressed:** same exact outer geometry and ornament positions as its
  matching normal asset. Slightly darken the face, reduce the raised bevel
  and glow, and make the inner face feel gently pressed inward.
- Make every pressed state clearly distinct while still looking enabled and
  unmistakably part of the same gold button family.
- Do not add a disabled, selected, loading, focus, or hover variation.

## Negative prompt

extra text, incorrect label, misspelled label, extra letters or numbers, logo,
watermark, signature, opaque background, full-screen UI, screenshot, phone
frame, clipped corners, cropped bevel,
stretched or compressed ornaments, decorative detail inside the text-safe
area, a different style for BACK, a different color for pressed, disabled
state, loading state, extra icons, extra buttons

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly six files exist with the specified names and pixel sizes.
- Confirm all are RGBA PNGs with transparency outside the button.
- Compare each normal/pressed pair as an overlay; their geometry must align.
- Confirm Short, Normal, and Long retain the same height and visual style,
  changing only their width and proportional center plate.
- Confirm the PNGs are text-free. Preview them in the game with their live
  labels (`BACK`, `NEXT LEVEL`, `RESTART MATCH`) in the existing dark, bold
  typeface; check centering and readability at target dp size.
- Preview all six assets against the dark Loadout footer and show each pair
  individually for review before Android integration.
